WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.587
A neural network does not normally calculate one connection at a time.

00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:12.492
It stores many weights inside matrices and applies them efficiently with matrix multiplication.

00:00:12.492 --> 00:00:15.547
The Python example uses pie torch.

00:00:15.547 --> 00:00:18.752
The input vector contains two values.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:23.632
W is a small weight matrix, and b is the bias vector.

00:00:23.632 --> 00:00:33.060
The expression X multiplied by W plus b produces the next representation, and Re L U applies the activation.

00:00:33.718 --> 00:00:36.045
Now compare the diagram on the right.

00:00:36.045 --> 00:00:41.300
A tiny neural network transforms numeric input with learned weights.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:49.835
An L L M does the same broad kind of numerical transformation at a much larger scale, using embedding weights,

00:00:49.835 --> 00:00:53.489
attention, feed-forward layers, and many Transformer blocks.
